Package: curvaUE
Title: Experimental Unit Dimensions from Bivariate CV Surfaces
Version: 0.3.3
Authors@R: c(
    person("Greivin", "Hernandez-Gonzalez", role = "aut"),
    person("Jorge Claudio", "Vargas-Rojas",
           role = "aut",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-1139-2148")),
    person("Juan Cruz", "Rodriguez",
           email = "jcrodriguez@unc.edu.ar",
           role = c("aut", "cre")))
Description: Estimates experimental-unit dimensions from uniformity trials using
    Gaussian and simultaneous sectional curvature, and a two-dimensional
    marginal-efficiency criterion, on a fitted bivariate
    coefficient-of-variation surface. Enumerates exact rectangular and square
    configurations with at least two experimental units, fits the Smith (1938)
    <doi:10.1017/S0021859600050516> weighted log-variance regression, and
    provides descriptive statistics, numerical results, and
    publication-ready figures. Analysis is performed
    in basic-unit coordinates; physical units are converted only afterwards.
